Makes Far Cry 2 sound closer to a serious shooter: rooms that ring like rooms, walls that muffle, gunshots with echoes, and distant fire that cracks.

[size=4][b]What it changes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]The game's own reverb, back[/b] - Far Cry 2 was authored with reverb for its buildings, jungle, savannah and desert, but it only ever played on an EAX sound card, which a modern PC does not have. The mod brings DSOAL along, which provides one in software, and the reverb now changes as you walk from place to place.[/*]
[*][b]A reverb that fits every building[/b] - the game picked one of four by hand, so a bus rang for seconds and many buildings had none. Each building now gets one by its type and size: small, medium and large rooms, a hall, a hangar and a ringing metal box. Shots in a small room have a short, hard slap off its walls.[/*]
[*][b]Walls that muffle by their material[/b] - concrete and mud walls muffle the outside most, sheds and shacks less, a bus with its open windows hardly at all. Open doors and windows let the outside in, so a house with its windows open is barely muffled while a closed one stays walled off.[/*]
[*][b]Your own pickups are never muffled[/b] - grabbing ammo in a safehouse no longer sounds as if it happened behind a wall.[/*]
[*][b]New gunshots[/b] - every single-player weapon, first and third person, from Dark Signal Weapon Soundscape. Full-auto weapons play a shot on every round.[/*]
[*][b]Echoes[/b] - every unsuppressed shot is followed by an echo, big or small by calibre, and enemies' shots echo too. In a burst only the last echo rings out.[/*]
[*][b]Distant fire that cracks[/b] - from about 40 m an enemy's shot turns into its crack and echo, and past 80 m the crack is all you hear.[/*]
[*][b]New grenade and rocket explosions[/b], close, medium and far.[/*]
[*][b]Voices that fall off like real speech[/b] - quieter by 20 m, gone by 50 m, instead of carrying across a camp.[/*]
[*][b]No more distant dogs and jackals[/b] in the ambience. Every other animal stays.[/*]
[*][b]A rougher, quieter idle[/b] for the Datsun pickup.[/*]
[*][b]A Combat music setting[/b] - in the [b]Mod Configuration[/b] menu. With it off, fights play without music so you can hear the enemy, and the calm music comes back when the fight is over. The game's own Music setting still turns all music off.[/*]
[/list]

With [b]DevTools[/b] installed, its overlay has a Sound Overhaul window that mutes single shots, full-auto fire or echoes, to hear the rest of a fight on its own.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/368]FCSE[/url], the plugin loader this runs in. Far Cry 2 1.03, Steam or GOG.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installing[/b][/size]

The download is a JackAll layer, which both installers read as-is:
[list]
[*][b]Vortex[/b] - with the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/2143]Far Cry 2 extension[/url] installed, drop the zip in and enable it.[/*]
[*][b]JackAll[/b] - add the zip in [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/370]JackAll[/url].[/*]
[/list]

DSOAL is never copied into the game's [b]bin[/b] folder: the plugin loads it from its own, and uninstalling the mod removes it.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]A dsound.dll already in bin[/b], such as DSOAL installed by hand, stays in charge, and the bundled one is not loaded.[/*]
[*][b]Weapon and sound mods[/b] that replace the same weapons' sounds, the explosions, the voice falloff or the reverb presets conflict. Whichever loads last wins.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Gunshots, echoes and explosions: [b]Dark Signal Weapon Soundscape[/b] (DSWS), by Dark Signal's original producer, with assets from [b]JSRS[/b].[/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/kcat/dsoal]DSOAL[/url] and [url=https://github.com/kcat/openal-soft]OpenAL Soft[/url], by Chris Robinson, under the LGPL-2.1. Their licenses ship beside them in the download.[/*]
[/list]
